1
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,560
O'er the glad waters of the dark blue sea,

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,540
Our thoughts as boundless, and our souls as free,

3
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:13,180
Far as the breeze can bear, the billows foam,

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,840
Survey our empire, and behold our home!

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,400
These are our realms, no limits to their sway—

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:24,700
Our flag the sceptre all who meet obey.

7
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,700
Ours the wild life in tumult still to range

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,440
From toil to rest, and joy in every change.

9
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:37,460
Oh, who can tell? not thou, luxurious slave!

10
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:41,440
Whose soul would sicken o'er the heaving wave;

11
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:44,780
Not thou, vain lord of Wantonness and Ease!

12
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:48,620
Whom Slumber soothes not—Pleasure cannot please—

13
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,880
Oh, who can tell, save he whose heart hath tried,

14
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:56,800
And danced in triumph o'er the waters wide,

15
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:00,340
The exulting sense—the pulse's maddening play,

16
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,700
That thrills the wanderer of that trackless way?

